WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.120
2007's coming-of-age comedy Superbad provided
a treasure trove of one-liners, hilarious

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:08.080
moments, and unforgettable characters.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:12.530
But it's hard to argue that there's anyone
more iconic than the fake-ID-sporting uber-geek,

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:13.530
McLovin.

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:18.350
The role even earned then 17-year-old actor
Christopher Mintz-Plasse an MTV Movie Award

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:20.260
nom for Best Breakthrough Performance.

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:23.940
While Superbad certainly helped springboard
some of its actors onto bigger and better

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.920
things, we haven't seen too much of Mintz-Plasse
lately.

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.400
Let's find out what adult McLovin looks like
today.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.380
"I am McLovin."

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.320
Becoming Fishlegs

00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:37.860
Not many people realize that Mintz-Plasse
is a prominent voice in the How to Train Your

00:00:37.860 --> 00:00:39.200
Dragon franchise.

00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:44.430
In 2010's action-fantasy, Mintz-Plasse voiced
the enthusiastic Fishlegs, a young viking

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:49.480
whose bulky body appears in sharp contrast
to the actor's skinny McLovin voice.

00:00:49.480 --> 00:00:54.240
"Hi, I'm Fishlegs. I've heard a lot about you. Clearly not enough."

00:00:54.640 --> 00:00:58.480
Mintz-Plasse digs doing voice work for family-friendly
fare, telling Hypable,

00:00:58.480 --> 00:00:59.910
"I love it, man.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:03.899
It's exciting because most of my movies are
rated R, and I go in there and I'm trying

00:01:03.899 --> 00:01:06.560
to make kids laugh, so it's cool to do a PG
movie.

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:09.969
And you can go in wearing sweatpants and do
it."

00:01:09.969 --> 00:01:11.549
Kick-ass moves

00:01:11.549 --> 00:01:16.899
Mintz-Plasse's second most famous role is
that of superhero-turned-supervillain, Chris

00:01:16.899 --> 00:01:20.569
"Red Mist" D'Amico, in Kick-Ass and Kick-Ass
2.

00:01:20.569 --> 00:01:23.440
That is, until his character changed his name.

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:27.140
"Henceforth, I'll be known as The Motherf---er."

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:32.130
The big-screen role was actually written with
Mintz-Plasse in mind, but the actor thinks

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.990
the original character from the Marvel comic
is cooler.

00:01:34.990 --> 00:01:35.990
He told CinemaBlend,

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:37.859
"[He's] much cooler than I am.

00:01:37.859 --> 00:01:41.740
They wanted my father to be a badass, and
I've never been accepted by him.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:45.539
They wanted that instead of the cool guy who's
always smoking and getting the girls."

00:01:45.539 --> 00:01:51.740
Nevertheless, the role landed Mintz-Plasse
a nomination at the 2010 Teen Choice Awards.

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:52.740
Hollywood remake

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:58.689
In 2011, Mintz-Plasse landed the role of "Evil
Ed" Lee in the comedic remake of 1985's horror

00:01:58.689 --> 00:01:59.770
flick, Fright Night.

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:05.250
"I really hate to be the one to tell you this,
but that guy your neighbor, yeah, he's a vampire."

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:08.720
Originally, Mintz-Plasse wasn't feeling a
reboot, but he couldn't pass up the chance

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:10.629
to work with Colin Farrell.

00:02:10.629 --> 00:02:11.629
Mintz-Plasse told HitFix,

00:02:11.629 --> 00:02:15.610
"I'm not the biggest fan of remakes, cuz I
sit and watch the trailers and I'm like, 'God,

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:18.030
just think of a new freakin idea,' y'know?"

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.970
But, he was on board once he saw the cast
list.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:24.069
"I saw that Anton and Colin and Greg and Craig
were all attached."

00:02:24.069 --> 00:02:27.549
"If done right it could be this really memorable
role for the movie."

00:02:27.549 --> 00:02:29.430
Almost a sitcom star

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:35.569
In 2012, Mintz-Plasse was on track to have
his own TV series, Friend Me, by writer Alan

00:02:35.569 --> 00:02:36.569
Kirschenbaum.

00:02:36.569 --> 00:02:40.620
Unfortunately, Friend Me was canceled after
Kirschenbaum passed away.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:41.620
Mintz-Plasse tweeted,

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:42.680
"RIP Alan.

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:46.450
Only [worked] with you for 10 days, but thanks
so much for this wonderful job.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:48.220
You were a funny, great guy."

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:52.870
But Mintz-Plasse landed on TV for real, when
he booked 2016's The Great Indoors.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:53.870
"Jack Gordon?

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:58.230
It is so incredible to meet you, I'm Clark,
online content curator."

00:02:58.230 --> 00:03:00.720
"Hi, Clark, obviously made up job title!"

00:03:00.720 --> 00:03:04.560
While the show was cancelled after just one
season, Mintz-Plasse's performance proved

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:07.719
he could be sitcom gold in the right part.

00:03:07.719 --> 00:03:08.719
Musically inclined

00:03:08.719 --> 00:03:11.990
Mintz-Plasse has appeared in a slew of music
videos.

00:03:11.990 --> 00:03:17.540
Perhaps most notably, he played drums in Kid
Cudi's late-'60s-inspired "Erase Me."

00:03:17.540 --> 00:03:22.200
Mintz-Plasse also appeared alongside Kick-Ass
costar Chloë Grace Moretz for The Soft Pack's

00:03:22.200 --> 00:03:27.069
"Answer to Yourself," as well as Unknown Mortal
Orchestra's "So Good At Being in Trouble."

00:03:27.069 --> 00:03:31.871
Most recently, he starred as a kidnapper in
Alison Wonderland's "U Don't Know," and as

00:03:31.871 --> 00:03:36.620
a man who overcomes life in a wheelchair,
in Kodaline's "Ready."

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:38.510
Rocking out

00:03:38.510 --> 00:03:40.909
Mintz-Plasse isn't just music video eye-candy.

00:03:40.909 --> 00:03:42.370
He's also in a band.

00:03:42.370 --> 00:03:46.660
After playing drums for Young Rapscallions
for eight years before they broke up, Mintz-Plasse

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:51.609
and his friend Adam Aseraf say they started
getting high, jamming out in the backyard,

00:03:51.609 --> 00:03:53.950
and calling themselves Bear on Fire.

00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:57.689
When they realized that things were getting
groovy, the duo recruited some friends and

00:03:57.689 --> 00:04:00.109
released their first studio album in 2015.

00:04:00.109 --> 00:04:04.700
Though shouts for "McLovin" inevitably follow
the actor wherever he plays, Mintz-Plasse

00:04:04.700 --> 00:04:05.700
doesn't mind.

00:04:05.700 --> 00:04:06.700
He told Stereogum,

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:10.440
"I just want as many people to come to the
show and as many people to hear my music as

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:12.100
possible."

00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.540
Going dark

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:18.280
When it comes to future work, Mintz-Plasse
is most interested in darker, more dramatic

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:19.280
roles.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:23.350
However, going dark in the Kick-Ass series
wasn't the easiest thing for the actor.

00:04:23.350 --> 00:04:24.760
He told The Belfast Telegraph,

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:29.230
"I read the script, and I was nervous because
it's unlike anything I've ever done before,

00:04:29.230 --> 00:04:30.640
so I got an acting coach.

00:04:30.640 --> 00:04:34.760
A month before filming, we would go through
every scene and every line and figure out

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:36.780
where the character needed to go emotionally."

00:04:36.780 --> 00:04:40.660
Mintz-Plasse also studied some other villainous
characters from the big-screen to help him

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:41.880
get it right.

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:43.700
And some from real life, too.

00:04:43.700 --> 00:04:44.700
He said,

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:48.730
"I watched Heath Ledger's Joker quite a bit,
and I researched [Marvel's] The Punisher.

00:04:48.730 --> 00:04:53.940
I [also] watched this really dark serial killer
on trial—I studied his eyes and how lifeless

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:55.800
they were and tried to use that too."

00:04:55.800 --> 00:05:00.940
A far cry from McLovin's innocent baby face,
but these days, he truly wants to kick some

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:01.940
ass.

00:05:01.940 --> 00:05:02.940
Thanks for watching!

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.170
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:05.170 --> 00:05:07.280
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

